WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.639
You know those stories that just live in your brain rent-free, like family legends, historical facts?
你知道那些免费存在于你大脑中的故事吗，比如家族传说、历史事实？

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:11.519
The kind of thing everybody swears is true because we've heard it all a million times.
每个人都发誓这是真的，因为我们已经听过一百万次了。

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:19.839
And then one day someone starts asking questions and suddenly the story gets a little wobbly.
然后有一天，有人开始提出问题，故事突然变得有点不稳定。

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:24.272
That's the idea behind the new podcast, Family Lore.
这就是新播客《Family Lore》背后的想法。

00:00:24.272 --> 00:00:29.150
It's a podcast that takes those big inherited narratives and pulls them apart.
这是一个播客，将那些继承下来的大故事分解开来。

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:35.280
Not to dismantle them just for the sake of it, but to better understand the whole making of story.
不是为了拆解它们，而是为了更好地理解故事的整个制作过程。

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.972
Coming up, we've got a preview of the family lore episode titled If Mosquito Hawks Can Fly.
接下来，我们将预览名为“如果蚊鹰会飞”的家庭传说剧集。

00:00:40.972 --> 00:00:47.289
It follows one family's story claiming that their grandfather took flight before the Wright brothers.
故事讲述了一个家庭的故事，声称他们的祖父在莱特兄弟之前就飞行了。

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:48.164
Take a listen.
听听。

00:00:48.164 --> 00:00:53.981
You might remember back in 1999, the United States Mint started producing specialty quarters.
您可能还记得 1999 年，美国造币厂开始生产特种 25 美分硬币。

00:00:53.981 --> 00:01:03.551
On the back of each quarter, instead of an eagle spreading its wings and looking off to the side, you'd see a unique design representing any given state.
在每枚硬币的背面，您会看到代表任何特定状态的独特设计，而不是一只张开翅膀向侧面看的老鹰。

00:01:03.551 --> 00:01:08.492
For example, on the back of the Massachusetts quarter, you'd have a minute man.
例如，在马萨诸塞州四分之一区的后面，你会有一个小人。

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:12.620
The Virginia quarter featured ships arriving at Jamestown in 1607.
弗吉尼亚区有 1607 年抵达詹姆斯敦的船只。

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:21.314
And on the back of the North Carolina quarter, you had a man lying prostrate on a primitive airplane, with another man watching from below.
在北卡罗来纳州四分之一区的后面，有一个人躺在一架原始的飞机上，另一个人在下面观看。

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:29.069
This, of course, was a depiction of of the Wright brothers and their inaugural flight at the small beach town of Kitty Hawk.
当然，这是对莱特兄弟和他们在海滨小镇基蒂霍克的首次飞行的描述。

00:01:29.069 --> 00:01:33.670
At the top of the coin is the inscription, First Flight.
硬币顶部刻有“首次飞行”字样。

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.549
This is a story that virtually all Americans know.
这是几乎所有美国人都知道的故事。

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:38.670
The Wright brothers were the first to fly.
莱特兄弟是第一个飞行的人。

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.829
The Wright brothers invented the airplane.
莱特兄弟发明了飞机。

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:45.750
Or at the very least, the Wright brothers were pioneers in the field of aviation.
或者至少，莱特兄弟是航空领域的先驱。

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:53.689
But there's another story you probably haven't heard that makes the origins of American aviation a little more complex.
但还有一个您可能没有听说过的故事，它使美国航空业的起源变得更加复杂。

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:55.989
I'm Lloyd Lockridge.
我是劳埃德·洛克里奇。

00:01:55.989 --> 00:02:05.959
And this is Family Lore.
这就是家族传说。

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:10.860
This story begins in Louisiana, a state not known for aviation.
这个故事始于路易斯安那州，一个不以航空闻名的州。

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.419
Quite the opposite, really.
事实恰恰相反。

00:02:12.419 --> 00:02:19.020
With its bayous swamps, labyrinthine coastline, and the nation's biggest river, the state is known for its boats.
该州拥有海湾沼泽、迷宫般的海岸线和全国最大的河流，以其船只而闻名。

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:19.665
Cajun P.
卡津·P。

00:02:19.665 --> 00:02:24.830
Rogues, flat-bottom airboats, paddle steamers, the Higgins boat.
盗贼号、平底汽艇、明轮船、希金斯船。

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:30.150
But the Louisiana man at the center of this episode's family lore was not interested in boats.
但本集家族传说中的路易斯安那男子对船不感兴趣。

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.669
He was not interested in navigating the water.
他对在水中航行不感兴趣。

00:02:32.669 --> 00:02:38.629
the advent of airplanes, this man dreamed of navigating the sky.
飞机出现后，这个人梦想着遨游天空。

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:41.981
His name was Charles Frederick Page.
他的名字叫查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇。

00:02:41.981 --> 00:02:55.669
And to hear his story, we have traveled to Alexandria, Louisiana in person to speak with one of his descendants, Charles Frederick Page's grandson.
为了听听他的故事，我们亲自前往路易斯安那州亚历山大，与他的后裔之一、查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇的孙子交谈。

00:02:55.669 --> 00:02:57.266
Joseph Page is 87 years old.
约瑟夫·佩奇今年 87 岁。

00:02:57.266 --> 00:03:01.827
He's a veteran of the United States Air Force and his military background shows.
他是美国空军的一名退伍军人，其军事背景可见一斑。

00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:04.392
His house is tidier than a nuclear submarine.
他的房子比核潜艇还整洁。

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:11.519
And Mr. Page stands with a certain posture, one that conveys not only physical strength, but a kind of strength of character.
佩奇先生以某种特定的姿势站立，这种姿势不仅传达了身体的力量，而且传达了一种性格的力量。

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:17.733
He's the kind of person who, without saying a word, makes you want to take your hat off when you walk inside.
他是那种不用说一句话就让你一走进去就想脱掉帽子的人。

00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:20.469
We were greeted by him and his wife of 65 years.
他和他结婚 65 年的妻子迎接了我们。

00:03:20.469 --> 00:03:26.000
We sat down in his living room and immediately launched into a conversation about his early life.
我们坐在他的客厅里，立即开始谈论他的早年生活。

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Well, I grew up on hybrid 20s in Pineville, so we lived in a country and about a hundred yards away.
嗯，我是在派恩维尔长大的，20 岁左右，所以我们住在一个乡村，距离我们大约一百码。

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:41.060
Joseph came of age in 1950s Louisiana, an overtly and unapologetically racist environment.
约瑟夫在 20 世纪 50 年代的路易斯安那州长大，那里是一个明显且毫无歉意的种族主义环境。

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:48.500
Despite living in Pineville, he had to commute across the Red River to Alexandria in order to attend the only all-black school in the area.
尽管住在派恩维尔，他必须穿过红河到达亚历山大，才能上该地区唯一的全黑人学校。

00:03:48.500 --> 00:04:01.151
And to add insult to injury, even if he were the first person at the municipal bus stop, he'd have to wait for all the white passengers to board first, only to pass them all on his way to the back of the bus.
更雪上加霜的是，即使他是第一个到达市政巴士站的人，他也必须等待所有白人乘客先上车，然后才能在到达巴士后部的路上超越他们。

00:04:01.151 --> 00:04:04.009
Indigities like that were a part of daily life.
像这样的数字是日常生活的一部分。

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:15.505
And this kind of blatant discrimination was a confusing experience for young Joseph Page, because his neighbors out in the country were white, and he'd play with his neighbors all the time.
对于年轻的约瑟夫·佩奇来说，这种公然的歧视是一次令人困惑的经历，因为他在乡下的邻居都是白人，而他总是和邻居一起玩。

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:22.195
But if they saw each other in the town of Alexandria, they'd have to pretend like they didn't know each other.
但如果他们在亚历山大镇见到对方，就必须假装不认识。

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.446
I didn't quite understand as a child.
我小时候不太明白。

00:04:24.446 --> 00:04:32.170
In my mind, I knew it was not right as to why we could be friends and hang out together in the country where nobody was around.
在我看来，我知道我们为什么能成为朋友并在一个无人的国家一起出去玩是不对的。

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:36.428
But we could not associate with each other when we were in Alexandria.
但我们在亚历山大时却无法交往。

00:04:36.428 --> 00:04:40.625
And as a child, do you remember thinking this doesn't make any sense?
当你还是个孩子的时候，你还记得你认为这没有任何意义吗？

00:04:40.625 --> 00:04:41.355
Yeah, I did.
是的，我做到了。

00:04:41.355 --> 00:04:42.571
Something was wrong.
出了点问题。

00:04:42.571 --> 00:04:44.882
I couldn't exactly put my hands on it.
我无法完全把手放在上面。

00:04:44.882 --> 00:04:56.560
But by the time I got to junior high school, I knew for a fact it was wrong and I recognized it as discrimination." Joseph was grappling with these issues in the midst of a national reckoning.
但当我上初中时，我知道这是错误的，我认为这是歧视。”约瑟夫在全国清算中努力解决这些问题。

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:03.008
The Civil Rights Act of 1964 was on the horizon and the movement for racial equality was gaining momentum.
1964 年《民权法案》即将出台，种族平等运动势头强劲。

00:05:03.008 --> 00:05:06.840
But Joseph had no illusions about the reality of his situation.
但约瑟夫对自己的现实处境并不抱任何幻想。

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:15.286
Despite the promises of civil rights, Joseph's parents told him that he'd need to work twice as hard as white people to achieve the same results.
尽管有公民权利的承诺，约瑟夫的父母告诉他，他需要比白人加倍努力才能取得同样的结果。

00:05:15.286 --> 00:05:17.279
And this was not some abstract lesson.
这并不是什么抽象的教训。

00:05:17.279 --> 00:05:25.166
It was inextricably connected to the story of the family's patriarch, Joseph's grandfather, Charles Frederick Page.
它与家族族长、约瑟夫的祖父查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇的故事有着千丝万缕的联系。

00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:29.212
Charles Page was born in 1864 in Rapides Parish, Louisiana.
查尔斯·佩奇 (Charles Page) 1864 年出生于路易斯安那州拉皮兹教区。

00:05:29.212 --> 00:05:41.350
He was born into slavery, which means that Joseph Page's grandfather, not his great-great-grandfather, or some distant relative, but his grandfather was, at one point, enslaved.
他出生在奴隶制家庭，这意味着约瑟夫·佩奇的祖父，不是他的曾曾祖父，也不是他的某个远房亲戚，而是他的祖父，曾经一度被奴役过。

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.021
I said I saw my grandchildren now.
我说我现在看到我的孙子了。

00:05:44.021 --> 00:05:48.500
She underscored a point of slavery was not that long ago.
她强调奴隶制问题不久前才出现。

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.590
Think about that.
想想看。

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:56.519
So tell me what one of the first things you remember learning about your grandfather Charles Frederick Page?
那么请告诉我，关于你的祖父查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇，你记得的第一件事是什么？

00:05:56.519 --> 00:06:01.973
Well my parents and my aunt and uncles always talked about it when I was a small kid.
当我还是个小孩子的时候，我的父母和我的阿姨和叔叔们总是谈论它。

00:06:01.973 --> 00:06:05.373
He was a bigger than life figure in my mind as a kid.
当我还是个孩子的时候，他在我心目中是一个比生命更伟大的人物。

00:06:05.373 --> 00:06:43.548
They always told us about inventing in the first airship in case he didn't catch that Joseph said that he was always told that his grandfather invented the first airship had we would go as school kids would do we would go to school to elementary school and say my grandfather built the first airship and the other kids were laughing at us and said you know that's not right the right brothers built the first airplane so as a kid you know when we're embarrassed by your friends right This claim that Charles Frederick Page invented an airship prior to the Wright Brothers inventing the airplane.
他们总是告诉我们有关发明第一艘飞艇的事，以防他没有听清楚约瑟夫说，他总是被告知他的祖父发明了第一艘飞艇，如果我们像小学生一样去学校，我们会去上小学，说我的祖父建造了第一艘飞艇，其他孩子嘲笑我们，说你知道这是不对的，正确的兄弟建造了第一架飞机，所以当你还是个孩子的时候，你知道当我们被你的朋友感到尴尬时，对吧查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇发明了这种说法莱特兄弟发明飞机之前的飞艇。

00:06:43.548 --> 00:06:46.371
This was a strong piece of Page family lore.
这是佩奇家族的一个重要传说。

00:06:46.371 --> 00:06:49.322
It's something the family believes to be true.
家人都相信这是真的。

00:06:49.322 --> 00:06:52.209
But a lot of people outside the family are...
但很多家庭之外的人...

00:06:52.209 --> 00:06:53.428
skeptical, at best.
充其量是持怀疑态度。

00:06:53.428 --> 00:06:57.598
Those who knew Charles Page respected him, but for other reasons.
认识查尔斯·佩奇的人都尊重他，但出于其他原因。

00:06:57.598 --> 00:06:59.202
He was a Renaissance man.
他是一位文艺复兴时期的人。

00:06:59.202 --> 00:07:02.410
He was a timberman, a cobbler, a botanical farmer.
他是一名伐木工人、一名鞋匠、一名植物种植者。

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:09.339
He established a cemetery for the Black community in Pineville, the first of its kind, the Lincoln Cemetery.
他在派恩维尔为黑人社区建立了第一个墓地——林肯公墓。

00:07:09.339 --> 00:07:14.899
He had a vision for diversified farming, where a tenant farmer could slowly gain equity in the land he was working.
他有一个多元化农业的愿景，让佃农可以慢慢获得他正在耕种的土地的股权。

00:07:14.899 --> 00:07:20.470
But what a lot of his peers didn't know is that he also had a mind for engineering.
但他的许多同行不知道的是，他也有工程头脑。

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.230
He would have been a great engineer.
他本来会成为一名伟大的工程师。

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:29.310
Grandmother used to complain about when she would tell my grandfather, she needed to do chicken coop.
祖母过去常常抱怨她什么时候会告诉祖父，她需要做鸡舍。

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:32.069
He needed to build her new chicken coop.
他需要为她建造新鸡舍。

00:07:32.069 --> 00:07:39.189
He would get out the ruler, and a pencil, and paper, and he would design it, and he would do all this stuff.
他会拿出尺子、一支铅笔和一张纸，他会设计它，他会做所有这些事情。

00:07:39.189 --> 00:07:41.689
It was like, all I need is a simple chicken coop.
就像，我所需要的只是一个简单的鸡舍。

00:07:41.689 --> 00:07:48.160
It did not have to be perfect, you know.
你知道，它不必是完美的。

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.379
But Charles Page had bigger ambitions than state-of-the-art chicken coops.
但查尔斯·佩奇有比最先进的鸡舍更大的野心。

00:07:52.379 --> 00:07:59.100
And one evening, while sitting on his porch, he got an idea from an unlikely contributor, the Mosquito Hawk.
一天晚上，当他坐在门廊上时，他从一位不太可能做出贡献的蚊鹰那里得到了一个想法。

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:05.399
Those big, gangly, slow-moving, mosquito-looking insects that you tend to see in the spring and fall.
那些大而细长、移动缓慢、看起来像蚊子的昆虫，你通常在春天和秋天看到。

00:08:05.399 --> 00:08:14.519
The story I heard repeatedly was that he was sitting on his porch in the evenings and watched the flight of those mosquito hogs.
我反复听到的故事是，他晚上坐在门廊上，看着那些蚊子飞走。

00:08:14.519 --> 00:08:24.350
And that inspired him to figure out how he could duplicate that and fly himself and figure out how to do that.
这激发了他思考如何复制这一点并自己飞行，并弄清楚如何做到这一点。

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:28.470
And in the ensuing weeks, months, or even years, nobody knows for sure.
在接下来的几周、几个月甚至几年里，没有人确切知道。

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:31.079
Charles Page worked on a way to fly.
查尔斯·佩奇研究了一种飞行方法。

00:08:31.079 --> 00:08:32.600
And he had a deadline.
他有一个最后期限。

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:40.352
He needed to design and build something in time for the 1904 Louisiana Purchase Exposition, which was held in St.
他需要为 1904 年在圣路易斯举行的路易斯安那购买博览会及时设计和建造一些东西。

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:41.450
Louis, Missouri.
密苏里州路易斯。

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:52.110
To hear the full episode and to learn more of Charles Frederick Page's role in the pioneering days of aviation, search for Family Lore wherever you get your podcasts.
要收听完整剧集并了解更多关于查尔斯·弗雷德里克·佩奇在航空先驱时代所扮演的角色，请在任何播客中搜索《Family Lore》。

